:::tab-content[tab=main width=880 align=center]

::::toolbar
- button[icon=chevron-left style=circled action=backToSettings tooltip="Back to Settings"]
- text[value="Archive"]
::::

Archived items are hidden from lists and search by default, but nothing is deleted.

::::row[icon=doc href=# trailing-label="Unarchive" trailing-action=unarchiveItem]
Weekly ops reports (Jun)
Doc · archived Jul 12
::::

::::row[icon=task href=# trailing-label="Unarchive" trailing-action=unarchiveItem]
W3 close-out checklist
Task list · archived Jul 23
::::

:::

::

Unarchive is the single trailing action — it returns the item to its lists and search immediately; archiving is always reversible and never destructive (that is Trash's job). The Settings-root Archive row mirrors the live count ("2 items · hidden from lists and search"). When the list is empty the pane shows the muted note "Nothing archived." The title row is circled back + title only — no actions to convert (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11). At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the shell contract applies unchanged: sidebar behind the generated tab-bar + FAB, the 880px column full-width with edge padding, and the rows with their trailing Unarchive action flow full-width and stay visible at touch widths.
